<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>CSS Cascade and Selector Priority</title>

    <style>
        p {
            color: blue;
        }
        .text {
            color: green;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>CSS Cascade and Selector Priority</h1>
    <p>This paragraph uses the element selector.</p>
    <p class="text">This paragraph uses the class selector.</p>
    <p id="special" class="text">
        This paragraph uses the ID selector, so it becomes orange.
    </p>
    <p id="inline" class="text"
       style="color: red;">
        This paragraph uses inline CSS, so it becomes red.
    </p>
    <h2>Selector Priority</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Element selector → Lowest priority</li>
        <li>Class selector → Higher priority</li>
        <li>ID selector → Higher priority than class</li>
        <li>Inline CSS → Very high priority</li>
        <li>!important → Highest priority</li>
    </ol>
</body>
</html>
